WEBVTT

00:19.776 --> 00:24.281
<i>Up until now, I thought I was the type
who gets along with everyone.</i>

00:24.948 --> 00:25.949
<i>Minato.</i>

00:26.032 --> 00:27.367
<i>But...</i>

00:27.451 --> 00:28.702
Hey, Hikawa.

00:29.828 --> 00:33.206
<i>My conversations
with her are always a little awkward.</i>

00:33.290 --> 00:35.542
We just finished morning practice.

00:36.251 --> 00:38.253
<i>Let's see, what is there to talk about?</i>

00:38.795 --> 00:40.964
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

00:41.048 --> 00:42.049
CRACK

00:42.132 --> 00:44.968
<i>Sheesh, that face.
Did I just step on a land mine?</i>

00:45.052 --> 00:46.428
WE HAD NO CONNECTION WHATSOEVER

00:46.511 --> 00:49.473
<i>Right, they don't seem all that close
and Igarashi looked a bit intense.</i>

00:49.556 --> 00:51.641
DIDN'T EXPECT THAT GORILLA TO GO
TO THIS SCHOOL - FOUL-MOUTHED?

00:51.725 --> 00:54.895
<i>Maybe she didn't vibe with him...
I messed up.</i>

00:55.479 --> 00:59.649
<i>Or maybe middle school is
a topic I need to avoid entirely.</i>

00:59.733 --> 01:00.901
<i>I should've been more tactful.</i>

01:02.069 --> 01:03.153
I'm sorry.

01:03.737 --> 01:06.490
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

01:07.491 --> 01:09.034
<i>No, that was awkward.</i>

01:09.117 --> 01:11.953
<i>This isn't going the way I'd hoped.</i>

01:12.037 --> 01:13.497
<i>We're getting nowhere.</i>

01:13.997 --> 01:17.125
<i>It's like the more I talk,
the deeper I sink...</i>

01:17.876 --> 01:19.127
<i>Huh?</i>

01:19.211 --> 01:21.421
<i>Was I always like this?</i>

01:26.510 --> 01:27.511
WARM AND TOASTY

01:27.594 --> 01:29.262
That cool air feels nice.

01:30.847 --> 01:31.848
Koyun--

01:31.932 --> 01:34.518
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

01:37.229 --> 01:38.688
I don't get it...

01:39.564 --> 01:41.483
<i>I thought I could hear...</i>

01:41.983 --> 01:43.026
You disgust me.

01:44.694 --> 01:46.404
<i>...the key to her heart locking me out.</i>

01:50.700 --> 01:53.120
Minato, what just...

01:53.203 --> 01:54.454
Wait, what happened?

01:54.538 --> 01:56.456
Yota, I think...

01:56.540 --> 01:59.209
Just don't go getting close
to Koyun for weird reasons.

02:00.335 --> 02:02.212
...Miki might kill me.

02:04.381 --> 02:05.382
What?

03:30.383 --> 03:35.931
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

03:36.514 --> 03:40.936
EPISODE 5
CHANGE

03:41.019 --> 03:43.438
NURSE'S OFFICE

03:43.521 --> 03:44.856
GLOOMY

03:44.940 --> 03:45.941
Good golly.

03:46.024 --> 03:47.442
KOYUKI IN THE NURSE'S OFFICE

03:47.525 --> 03:50.070
There you go, eating sweet bread
and calling it a meal...

03:50.153 --> 03:54.407
Noriko, is there a way to not get mad?

03:54.491 --> 03:57.661
- Wait, even someone like you gets mad?
- <i>Hot... Chilly...</i>

03:57.744 --> 03:59.037
I do.

03:59.120 --> 04:00.497
Did you get into a fight?

04:02.540 --> 04:06.461
Well, everyone gets upset sometimes.

04:06.544 --> 04:09.297
You don't have
to deal with things on your own.

04:10.882 --> 04:14.552
It'd be easier if I could lash out
and get it out of my system,

04:15.053 --> 04:17.722
but I'm not like that.

04:18.556 --> 04:20.809
I know that about myself, but...

04:21.851 --> 04:24.646
Actually, I end up regretting
saying something at all.

04:24.729 --> 04:25.730
I HATE MYSELF

04:25.814 --> 04:27.315
<i>She's a handful.</i>

04:27.816 --> 04:30.318
I don't know what happened,

04:30.402 --> 04:33.238
but it's important
to communicate how you feel.

04:33.321 --> 04:35.991
You have to use your words
if you don't like something.

04:36.074 --> 04:37.367
<i>Communicate?</i>

04:37.951 --> 04:38.952
<i>No.</i>

04:39.703 --> 04:43.248
<i>At that moment, I lost my temper...</i>

04:43.331 --> 04:44.582
You disgust me.

04:45.583 --> 04:47.085
<i>...and I meant to hurt him.</i>

04:48.086 --> 04:52.340
<i>Not only that, I lashed out at him
without hearing him out first.</i>

04:53.341 --> 04:55.260
<i>The lingering frustration</i>

04:55.343 --> 04:58.763
<i>and regret for my own actions
keep spinning in my head.</i>

05:00.849 --> 05:01.850
YUM-MELON

05:01.933 --> 05:02.934
All I want is peace.

05:03.018 --> 05:04.019
SIGH

05:04.102 --> 05:06.021
What're you saying?
You're still in your teens.

05:07.981 --> 05:09.190
There you are.

05:10.817 --> 05:14.029
Koyun! I'll eat here too.

05:14.112 --> 05:17.324
Good grief,
when'd my office turn into a café?

05:17.407 --> 05:18.700
Want some, Koyun?

05:18.783 --> 05:20.660
- No, thanks...
- Sheesh.

05:21.202 --> 05:22.787
What brings you here?

05:22.871 --> 05:26.541
Well, this morning,

05:26.624 --> 05:30.462
I overheard the conversation
between you guys by the entrance.

05:38.136 --> 05:39.596
I'M HERE
I NEED YOUR NAME AND CLASS

05:39.679 --> 05:41.598
Clean up your own mess
before you head out.

05:41.681 --> 05:42.807
- Will do.
- Okay.

05:42.891 --> 05:45.560
MAKING ROUNDS - PLEASE COME
TO THE TEACHER'S ROOM

05:46.186 --> 05:47.187
Say, Koyun.

05:47.729 --> 05:52.192
Minato doesn't understand personal space,
can be overbearing, has a big ego

05:52.275 --> 05:53.902
- and is surprisingly childish.
- Hey...

05:53.985 --> 05:56.154
He thinks the world revolves around him,

05:56.237 --> 05:58.156
but he's not a bad guy.

06:00.658 --> 06:02.952
Also, I need to come clean.

06:03.536 --> 06:06.831
Minato and I have known of you
since middle school.

06:07.582 --> 06:08.583
What?

06:09.167 --> 06:11.586
<i>Though, we didn't know your name.</i>

06:11.669 --> 06:15.507
<i>It hit me when you mentioned
you were in the basketball club.</i>

06:16.508 --> 06:18.968
Basketball club? How...

06:20.845 --> 06:25.183
Miki told us about how you were bullied.

06:28.686 --> 06:30.438
Morning, Koyun.

06:30.522 --> 06:33.775
For once, I got here with time to spare...

06:35.944 --> 06:39.114
What... the heck?

06:39.197 --> 06:40.323
Forget you saw anything.

06:40.406 --> 06:42.492
What do you mean, "Forget it"?

06:42.992 --> 06:44.285
Since when?

06:44.369 --> 06:46.788
Good question. The entire time?

06:49.165 --> 06:51.292
I can't wait for all this to end.

06:52.794 --> 06:55.588
Miki told you two...

06:55.672 --> 06:58.007
Please don't be angry with her.

06:58.091 --> 07:01.386
She was worried sick about you back then.

07:01.469 --> 07:02.971
Yeah, I understand.

07:03.054 --> 07:07.851
<i>Miki told us that she didn't realize
her friend was struggling.</i>

07:07.934 --> 07:10.770
<i>That she couldn't help her friend at all.</i>

07:11.271 --> 07:14.315
I keep thinking, "Why didn't she tell me?

07:14.816 --> 07:17.444
Am I that unreliable?"

07:18.236 --> 07:20.113
It makes me a little sad.

07:20.822 --> 07:23.158
It's not about you being unreliable.

07:23.241 --> 07:26.453
Maybe your friend
simply didn't want to worry you.

07:27.454 --> 07:29.372
You think so?

07:29.456 --> 07:30.457
SOB

07:30.540 --> 07:32.542
But I wish she was open with me!

07:32.625 --> 07:33.626
Miki!

07:34.252 --> 07:35.420
So...

07:35.503 --> 07:37.630
That's how it made her feel...

07:38.590 --> 07:40.633
<i>I didn't confide in Miki because...</i>

07:40.717 --> 07:42.427
Go, Miki!

07:43.720 --> 07:45.054
Nice!

07:45.138 --> 07:46.181
Gimme five!

07:46.264 --> 07:48.766
<i>...Miki took club activities seriously</i>

07:49.267 --> 07:52.061
<i>while I only attended practice</i>

07:52.145 --> 07:56.149
<i>out of the fear of quitting.
It felt like we were polar opposites.</i>

07:56.983 --> 08:01.988
<i>It was never about trust
or her being unreliable.</i>

08:04.449 --> 08:09.537
Minato must've pieced it together
when he saw the two of you.

08:09.621 --> 08:12.624
That you're the girl in the basketball
club Miki mentioned before.

08:13.124 --> 08:16.878
That must be why
Minato was concerned about you.

08:17.879 --> 08:18.922
<i>So that's it.</i>

08:20.465 --> 08:21.591
I'm sorry.

08:21.674 --> 08:23.927
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

08:24.511 --> 08:26.930
<i>That's why Amamiya said that...</i>

08:27.931 --> 08:31.017
<i>I completely misunderstood him, and I...</i>

08:31.100 --> 08:32.435
PARANOID - SELF-CONSCIOUS

08:34.312 --> 08:35.313
How embarrassing!

08:35.396 --> 08:36.397
Koyun?

08:37.190 --> 08:40.068
No, I must give him a sincere apology.

08:40.568 --> 08:43.154
A sincere apology? That's a bit heavy.

08:43.238 --> 08:45.198
Want me to be the messenger?

08:45.281 --> 08:47.867
No. I must express my apologetic intent.

08:47.951 --> 08:49.202
Apologetic intent?

08:49.827 --> 08:52.705
I guess he isn't too bothered.

08:53.289 --> 08:55.708
Don't worry about it.
Besides, it's only Minato.

08:56.834 --> 08:58.419
Hey, Amamiya!

09:00.547 --> 09:02.423
Sorry. Over here.

09:04.300 --> 09:06.386
Hello?

09:07.679 --> 09:11.474
What? Are you mad, Amamiya?

09:12.058 --> 09:14.143
Sorry, I was spacing out.

09:14.227 --> 09:15.228
What?

09:15.311 --> 09:17.313
You surprised me.

09:17.397 --> 09:19.649
I thought you were upset
for a second there.

09:19.732 --> 09:23.570
Idiot. Minato's got a resting cranky face.

09:25.572 --> 09:28.491
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

09:28.575 --> 09:33.538
<i>Did she say that
because I was talking with Igarashi?</i>

09:34.038 --> 09:36.749
<i>But is it that big of a deal?</i>

09:37.750 --> 09:41.838
<i>They say, "Don't do unto others
what you wouldn't have them do unto you."</i>

09:42.338 --> 09:44.507
<i>But the opposite isn't necessarily okay?</i>

09:45.300 --> 09:46.593
<i>I don't understand.</i>

09:47.093 --> 09:48.511
<i>Or rather...</i>

09:48.595 --> 09:50.888
<i>we're too different.</i>

09:50.972 --> 09:53.558
<i>We've got completely different values
and outlooks on life.</i>

09:54.350 --> 09:56.519
<i>What's right to me...</i>

09:57.854 --> 10:00.315
<i>and what's right to her are too different.</i>

10:01.107 --> 10:04.527
<i>So no matter what I do for her,
it ends up upsetting her.</i>

10:07.113 --> 10:11.284
<i>So trying to help makes me sanctimonious?</i>

10:11.367 --> 10:13.036
Is it, Miki?

10:14.495 --> 10:17.540
<i>If we're talking about sanctimonious,
then she is too.</i>

10:17.624 --> 10:21.794
<i>She draws a clear line between the people
she likes and those she doesn't.</i>

10:21.878 --> 10:24.464
<i>She accepts Yota and Miki.</i>

10:24.547 --> 10:27.050
<i>Meanwhile, I'm a reject.</i>

10:28.551 --> 10:29.552
MIFFED

10:29.636 --> 10:32.555
<i>It's starting to make me upset.</i>

10:32.639 --> 10:34.349
BOINK
WHOA - BAM

10:34.432 --> 10:35.933
What's the matter?

10:36.517 --> 10:39.437
<i>All right.
I won't bother with her anymore.</i>

10:39.520 --> 10:42.607
<i>It doesn't benefit either of us,
and it's not worth worrying about.</i>

10:42.690 --> 10:43.691
GRADE 1 CLASS 5

10:44.942 --> 10:45.943
Yota.

10:46.027 --> 10:48.738
Where were you during lunch?

10:50.531 --> 10:51.574
The bathroom?

10:51.658 --> 10:52.700
That long?

10:56.537 --> 11:00.458
<i>The day's over, but I couldn't find
the right time to apologize.</i>

11:01.042 --> 11:04.003
<i>Wait, is there such a thing
as a good time to apologize?</i>

11:04.087 --> 11:05.213
GOOD TIME TO APOLOGIZE

11:06.881 --> 11:09.258
<i>I hope I can catch him tomorrow.</i>

11:09.342 --> 11:10.718
See you, Minato.

11:10.802 --> 11:12.136
Bye.

11:31.030 --> 11:34.492
<i>This whole time, not once,</i>

11:34.575 --> 11:38.287
<i>have I given him a fair chance.</i>

11:39.330 --> 11:42.083
<i>I made assumptions based on
what happened in the past</i>

11:42.166 --> 11:44.752
<i>and decided from the start
that we don't vibe.</i>

11:45.503 --> 11:47.755
<i>I rejected him
without ever getting to know him.</i>

11:48.339 --> 11:52.510
<i>I did something I'd hate to go through
to someone else without a thought.</i>

11:58.850 --> 12:00.810
<i>That expression...</i>

12:00.893 --> 12:04.272
<i>It's the face she makes
when her guard is up.</i>

12:04.856 --> 12:08.067
<i>I thought we'd be friends in time,</i>

12:08.568 --> 12:11.028
<i>but that was just my ego talking.</i>

12:11.612 --> 12:12.864
<i>I was arrogant.</i>

12:13.364 --> 12:15.366
<i>To her, I was just a nuisance.</i>

12:15.992 --> 12:19.162
<i>Maybe it was better
if I never bothered her to begin with.</i>

12:19.245 --> 12:20.663
Amamiya!

12:21.247 --> 12:22.248
Huh?

12:24.709 --> 12:25.918
I'm sorry.

12:28.796 --> 12:32.425
Can we talk for a minute?

12:38.514 --> 12:40.892
Do you have time right now?

12:40.975 --> 12:43.978
Yeah. I've got time
to kill before my club starts.

12:46.147 --> 12:47.940
So...

12:48.524 --> 12:53.112
<i>What do I even say? I'm ashamed.
I'm ashamed about everything.</i>

12:53.196 --> 12:55.198
MISUNDERSTANDING
PARANOID - SELF-CONSCIOUS

12:56.657 --> 12:58.951
Sorry I was terrible to you.

12:59.452 --> 13:00.453
Okay.

13:00.536 --> 13:02.371
When you mentioned middle school,

13:02.455 --> 13:06.417
I was worried how you knew
what happened in middle school.

13:06.918 --> 13:11.797
Just thinking Igarashi told you
made my stomach churn.

13:12.632 --> 13:16.802
<i>But Yota told me during lunch today
that it was all just a misunderstanding.</i>

13:17.386 --> 13:18.387
Yota did?

13:21.933 --> 13:22.975
The bathroom?

13:23.059 --> 13:24.310
That guy...

13:25.102 --> 13:26.312
I...

13:26.896 --> 13:30.399
got ahead of myself,
and behaved poorly towards you.

13:30.900 --> 13:31.901
I...

13:32.944 --> 13:35.571
I... I...

13:35.655 --> 13:38.074
<i>Words overflow in my mind,</i>

13:38.574 --> 13:40.618
<i>but I can't ever find
the right way to get them out.</i>

13:40.701 --> 13:42.328
I WANT TO GIVE A PROPER APOLOGY
I WANT TO CHANGE

13:42.411 --> 13:43.829
FOR SELF-SATISFACTION?
FOR WHOSE SAKE?

13:43.913 --> 13:45.331
I WANT TO TELL HIM
TELL HIM WHAT?

13:45.414 --> 13:48.376
<i>When words race through my mind,
when I try to get them out,</i>

13:49.001 --> 13:51.462
<i>they get mixed up in my throat.</i>

13:51.546 --> 13:53.714
<i>All these feelings I can't put into words</i>

13:54.382 --> 13:56.425
<i>try to escape by turning into tears.</i>

13:57.468 --> 13:59.095
WHOA...!

13:59.178 --> 14:02.056
<i>Don't cry, don't cry, don't cry!</i>

14:02.139 --> 14:03.182
<i>Why do I always...</i>

14:03.266 --> 14:04.934
<i>I owe him an apology. I can't cry.</i>

14:05.017 --> 14:06.018
ONLY TEARING UP

14:06.102 --> 14:08.312
<i>Hold it in, hold it in, hold it in!</i>

14:08.396 --> 14:09.397
Hikawa.

14:10.022 --> 14:11.274
It's all right.

14:12.858 --> 14:15.194
You don't have to apologize profusely,

14:15.278 --> 14:17.405
and besides, I'm the one who troubled you.

14:17.488 --> 14:20.783
<i>As if. I was upset until a moment ago.</i>

14:20.866 --> 14:22.535
<i>Why am I the one consoling her?</i>

14:22.618 --> 14:24.912
You can let it out. What...

14:24.996 --> 14:26.914
TEARS FALLING

14:29.000 --> 14:31.544
<i>When someone is kind
as I'm holding back tears,</i>

14:32.295 --> 14:33.838
<i>it all comes out at once...</i>

14:34.505 --> 14:36.674
TEARS STREAMING DOWN

14:37.258 --> 14:38.301
<i>She's crying.</i>

14:39.886 --> 14:41.178
FRAYING - PILLING

14:41.262 --> 14:42.263
HIDE...

14:42.847 --> 14:44.181
I...

14:44.265 --> 14:45.766
IT ALL COMES FLOODING OUT
BAWLING

14:45.850 --> 14:48.436
I lied when I said
I don't have a connection with Igarashi.

14:48.519 --> 14:50.897
- What?
- Rather, it's the opposite.

14:51.647 --> 14:53.941
We don't get along anymore.

14:55.860 --> 14:57.987
Where are we carrying these to again?

14:58.070 --> 14:59.947
Turn left, then go straight.

15:02.033 --> 15:03.451
THEY'RE ALONE - CRYING

15:03.534 --> 15:04.702
BOUND TO BE MISUNDERSTOOD

15:05.786 --> 15:06.871
Hikawa.

15:09.290 --> 15:10.958
It's heavy.

15:11.667 --> 15:14.462
See this? What do you think?

15:14.962 --> 15:17.089
What're they doing?

15:17.173 --> 15:19.550
Maybe they found a rare monster.

15:20.551 --> 15:21.928
My parents are...

15:27.391 --> 15:28.726
Thank you.

15:31.395 --> 15:32.396
Who's this?

15:34.941 --> 15:36.317
It's my Pomeranian.

15:38.319 --> 15:39.737
<i>She laughed.</i>

15:42.073 --> 15:43.491
How cute.

15:48.162 --> 15:49.956
Well, I've gotta get going.

15:50.039 --> 15:51.165
Sorry.

15:51.248 --> 15:52.249
Bye.

15:55.378 --> 15:56.754
See you tomorrow.

15:57.380 --> 16:00.257
Okay. See you.

16:15.398 --> 16:18.025
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

16:18.609 --> 16:21.529
<i>Hikawa said
she doesn't get along with Igarashi...</i>

16:21.612 --> 16:23.406
<i>But back then...</i>

16:23.990 --> 16:26.283
Hey. Igarashi?

16:26.367 --> 16:28.035
Do you remember Hikawa?

16:32.164 --> 16:33.791
Hikawa?

16:33.874 --> 16:36.919
I don't remember anyone
by that name from middle school.

16:37.503 --> 16:38.504
<i>Wait...</i>

16:39.171 --> 16:40.631
<i>What does it all mean?</i>

16:41.132 --> 16:43.300
TODAY'S RECOMMENDATION
RAMEN FAIR

16:43.384 --> 16:45.302
RICE - BOWLS

16:45.386 --> 16:47.054
SPACING OUT

16:47.722 --> 16:50.141
<i>It didn't look like
either of them was lying.</i>

16:50.224 --> 16:51.767
Rather, it's the opposite.

16:51.851 --> 16:52.977
Who's that?

16:53.060 --> 16:55.062
<i>What happened between them?</i>

16:55.146 --> 16:57.481
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

16:57.565 --> 16:58.566
SNAPPING OUT

16:59.316 --> 17:00.735
DEFLATED

17:01.861 --> 17:03.529
Is something wrong, Amamiya?

17:04.655 --> 17:05.698
It's nothing.

17:05.781 --> 17:06.782
GRR!

17:06.866 --> 17:09.952
Liar! You've been spacing out
this entire time.

17:10.036 --> 17:11.037
I'm listening.

17:11.120 --> 17:13.497
Then what was I talking about? Tell me!

17:13.581 --> 17:14.957
Aren't you a needy girlfriend.

17:15.041 --> 17:16.125
WHAT YOU JUST SAID

17:16.208 --> 17:19.503
Minato, your noodles will get soggy
if you keep spacing out.

17:20.004 --> 17:23.090
- What inspired that combination?
- They don't go together, do they?

17:23.174 --> 17:24.550
They're yummy.

17:24.633 --> 17:26.510
- Gluten galore.
- What?

17:26.594 --> 17:27.595
<i>Yota.</i>

17:27.678 --> 17:30.681
Yota told me during lunch today
that it was all just a misunderstanding.

17:31.640 --> 17:34.268
<i>She calls him by his first name.</i>

17:34.769 --> 17:37.772
<i>With the exams out of the way,
we're heading into winter break.</i>

17:38.272 --> 17:39.940
<i>We'll have nothing in common...</i>

17:45.279 --> 17:46.280
SLURP

17:46.363 --> 17:48.949
- <i>So what?</i>
- In one go? You're creeping me out!

17:51.285 --> 17:55.206
<i>How will she react if I approach her
the next time we meet?</i>

17:55.873 --> 17:59.877
<i>Will she feel awkward?
Or will she keep a distance, like before?</i>

17:59.960 --> 18:00.961
EPISODE ONE

18:02.755 --> 18:04.215
<i>I'm out of ideas.</i>

18:07.301 --> 18:08.719
BA-BUMP

18:09.345 --> 18:10.805
Amamiya.

18:10.888 --> 18:11.972
BLUSH

18:17.561 --> 18:18.729
<i>What?</i>

18:18.813 --> 18:21.065
Yesterday,

18:21.816 --> 18:24.735
I'm sorry I ended up crying
when I was trying to apologize.

18:24.819 --> 18:27.071
I must've been a mess.

18:27.905 --> 18:29.240
ABSENT-MINDED

18:29.323 --> 18:33.202
It's not that I thought
you'd forgive me if I cried.

18:33.994 --> 18:34.995
Don't worry.

18:35.579 --> 18:38.541
Well, sometimes, we get overwhelmed

18:38.624 --> 18:42.253
and end up crying
for no good reason, right?

18:42.336 --> 18:43.337
DUMBFOUNDED

18:43.420 --> 18:45.631
It happens to you too?

18:46.799 --> 18:48.134
- So what?
- What?

18:48.717 --> 18:51.387
You thought I wouldn't
be able to understand?

18:51.470 --> 18:54.640
- What?
- That's terrible.

18:54.723 --> 18:55.724
SOB SOB

18:55.808 --> 18:56.892
FLUSTER FLUSTER

18:56.976 --> 18:58.310
To be honest, I didn't expect it.

18:58.394 --> 18:59.395
AH

18:59.979 --> 19:04.233
I may not look it,
but I'm a sensitive guy.

19:06.360 --> 19:07.403
What's that face for?

19:12.366 --> 19:13.617
You're so rude.

19:19.081 --> 19:21.584
Well, I'm going this way.

19:21.667 --> 19:23.669
- For your club?
- You guessed it.

19:25.296 --> 19:26.422
Good luck.

19:27.673 --> 19:28.674
Okay.

19:43.480 --> 19:47.443
<i>I shouldn't assume all the time
that people don't understand me</i>

19:47.526 --> 19:50.112
<i>or that they'll reject me.</i>

19:53.282 --> 19:55.576
MIKI - COME TO MY WORK
OVER WINTER BREAK - SEE YA

19:55.659 --> 19:59.413
<i>It's as if something changed
ever so slightly... or maybe not.</i>

19:59.496 --> 20:00.706
I'LL INVITE YOTA TOO

20:01.999 --> 20:03.292
<i>That's the vibe.</i>

20:03.792 --> 20:07.379
<i>Winter break starts tomorrow.</i>

21:39.013 --> 21:41.181
KAWAII CAFE - WELCOME
WINTER BREAK FAIR

21:41.765 --> 21:45.936
Miharu! Sora! It's been a hot minute. Yay!

21:46.020 --> 21:47.229
Yay!

21:47.313 --> 21:48.439
How've you been?

21:48.522 --> 21:49.857
CATCHING UP WITH OLD FRIENDS

21:49.940 --> 21:52.693
Haven't seen you since we graduated.
How's high school going?

21:52.776 --> 21:54.528
It's peaceful and nice.

21:54.611 --> 21:57.531
Well? Are you two dating anyone?

21:57.614 --> 21:59.366
- Nope.
- Same.

21:59.450 --> 22:00.701
<i>She didn't miss a beat.</i>

22:00.784 --> 22:04.330
You went through boys in middle school.

22:04.413 --> 22:07.958
Like that handsome upperclassman and
the volleyball guy from another school.

22:08.917 --> 22:10.711
Well, that was...

22:10.794 --> 22:12.338
AN UPPERCLASSMAN
WITH NO CONNECTION WHATSOEVER

22:12.421 --> 22:14.048
He asked me out all of a sudden.

22:14.131 --> 22:15.132
MIGHT AS WELL!

22:15.215 --> 22:17.968
He grew on me, so I said yes.

22:18.052 --> 22:21.221
Every time I go out with a guy,
they call it off

22:21.305 --> 22:23.474
because I'm not who they thought I'd be.

22:24.558 --> 22:25.559
GRRR!

22:25.642 --> 22:29.188
Don't go creating an ideal version of me
and then get disappointed!

22:29.271 --> 22:31.398
She went full gorilla mode.

22:31.482 --> 22:32.983
Hey, sorry.

22:33.067 --> 22:36.987
All I'm saying is,
it doesn't count as going out.

22:37.071 --> 22:40.491
Next time I go steady with someone,

22:41.116 --> 22:46.080
I want to be the one to ask him out.

22:46.163 --> 22:47.790
Is there a guy you're into?

22:47.873 --> 22:48.874
Nobody.

22:49.833 --> 22:51.460
<i>What about Amamiya?</i>

22:51.543 --> 22:54.379
<i>Bringing him up now
will only complicate things.</i>

22:54.880 --> 22:56.256
What about you, Koyuki?

22:56.340 --> 22:58.008
Any boys in your life, Koyuki?

22:59.218 --> 23:00.302
Me?

23:04.264 --> 23:05.265
No, thanks.

23:06.558 --> 23:09.686
I don't think I'm cut out
for relationships.

23:10.354 --> 23:14.274
I admire the both of you
for keeping it going with your boyfriends.

23:15.943 --> 23:17.611
It's not that big of a deal.

23:18.612 --> 23:20.030
Do you have any pics?

23:20.114 --> 23:21.406
HEE HEE

23:21.490 --> 23:22.783
Can I show you?

23:24.409 --> 23:26.620
Gotta head off to work. See you.

23:26.703 --> 23:27.788
- See you!
- Bye bye.

23:27.871 --> 23:29.206
Let's hang out again.

23:31.375 --> 23:34.169
Koyuki's got it rough.

23:34.670 --> 23:38.298
What can she do?
There's what happened with Igarashi.

23:39.341 --> 23:43.262
To begin with,
why did she go out with Igarashi

23:43.345 --> 23:46.098
in middle school?

23:47.099 --> 23:48.934
I thought she hated his guts.

23:49.017 --> 23:51.228
Yeah, it surprised me too.

23:51.311 --> 23:53.856
<i>I think I'm the one to blame.</i>

23:53.939 --> 23:55.941
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
